Probably none of you remember who I am; I posted here on occasion ages
ago (and got some useful info). But after many years of playing Nethack
off and on, I finally actually managed to ascend. I know ascension is
same-old same-old for most of you here, but for me success in Nethack
is as much a victory versus my own impatience as anything else. And
since is my first (and possibly my last :) ) ascension, I felt I needed
to

a) let out a public hurrah! (HURRAH!)
and
b) Thanks for those of you here who were helpful to me in the past.

Not-so-brief Summary

I played the game on NAO. I wanted to play a wizard just because I was
sick of playing bashers, and random genned the race/alignment. I can't
remember my starting equip completely, but I think I had a ring of
teleport, a ring of polymorph (which I never used, as you can see
below), a standard issue force bolt book, and a book of cure sickness
(I had the spell memorized, but I don't think I ever used it).

Early game was tough--original cat died early to an unseen falling rock
trap, so forced myself to play slow. Decided early on not to bother
slowing my leveling to try to more easily buy protection in the mines
early on, which I do sometimes with wizards; I'd rather fight and level
up and have hit points and improve my AC in other ways first. This
turned out to be a good decision.

Earliest bit of luck was I found a cornuthaum in a armor store. Was
_very_ careful to properly ID it, as I've screwed myself over before
with dunce caps. This helped me out a lot.

Had some insane luck with bones files--nice thing about playing on a
public server, I guess. I found no less than three of the remains of my
brother wizards, and fortunately whatever killed them in most cases
were gone (I think two were killed "while helpless" by ordinary
things). The first I found in the mines with Magicbane on him--cursed,
yeah, but that was easily taken care of. The others had some good
spellbooks. I think by the time I looted the third dead wizard, far,
far deeper into the Dungeons (if not lower), I had Charm Monster, which
I think saved my life against a number of enemy spellcasters who
summoned hordes of monsters. In Genhennom I found a *fourth* bones file
of a fallen Valkyrie, I think, with Vorpal Blade and the Orb of Fate.
Alignment prevented me from taking the Orb, but I managed to pick up
Vorpy--yeah, alignment blasting on occasion, but it beheaded Asmodeus,
Baalzebub, and Yeenoghu, so I'm not complaining. I alternated between
Magicbane and Vorpal Blade depending on what I was fighting--usually
stuck to Magicbane, but Vorpal Blade was best for bosses.

Bones files also got me a few magic markers and a bag of holding. One
had a magic lamp which I blessed and wished for Silver Dragon Scale
Mail, a livesaver. THis allowed me to lose the amulet of reflection
from Sokoban and switch out to an amulet of magical breathing, and then
for a time to the Eye of Aethiopica after I wrested that from the Dark
One's hands. (I tended to swap between the two amulets as I felt
necessary.)

Found an aligned priest in the Dungeons and paid him off from time to
time for Protection. It was expensive but I had no other use for the
gold.

Charged the castle wand to 3 wishes. Didn't use them right away. After
being attacked by two master liches and an arch-lich between the castle
and the Land of the Dead (surviving mostly by charming the enemies they
summoned), I wished for a blessed scroll of genocide and got rid of all
Ls. If nothing else, they were making me impatient with the game, and
impatience is bad. I think one of my wishes was for a scroll of
charging--maybe to charge a magic marker so I could enchant my armor
better.

I found a book of Finger of Death on the Medusa level. This thing made
the game almost too easy--until it was time for me to fight the Wizard,
in which it seemed to be the difference between life and death at
times. Eventually I used my last wish to get another book of Finger of
Death when I accidentally lost the first one after falling in some
water (stupid keyboard... it was its fault entirely, I'm sure. THe
second two times that I fell into the water I admit were my fault,
though).

Had weird pet luck--lots of them died or, at careless moments, killed
in the crossfire when I was tackled by lots of enemies. For awhile,
though, had two pet Jabberwocks, a pet Red Dragon, pet Green Dragon,
and a pet Fire Elemental. I was surprised--the Fire Elemental was
actually very helpful, as much as the others. I think they all
eventually bit it either on the bottom level on my run upstairs after
retrieving the amulet, and at that point I'd lost knowledge of the
spell and had lost the spellbook, so didn't bother further with pets.

Found the Amulet somewhere randomly on the floor in the bottom level.
Decided not to question that, and ran back up. Had a _heck_ of a time
getting up the stairs in the dungeon--kept teleporting me back down for
awhile. I actually checked some spoilers to see what was causing that,
but it turns out just being chaotic causes the likelihood of that to
happen increase. The things you learn.

Didn't seem to get attacked by Rodney that often (9 times--but honestly
I expected more). I'd lost most of my scrolls of gold detection due to
the water dive, but I'd found a crystal ball somewhere so used that to
find the traps. Air Elementals seemed to cause me the most trouble.
They hurt!

Astral Plane made me a nervous wreck. I wore the Amulet of Life Saving
here and was surprised I never needed it. Gave Famine and Pestilence
the Finger a few times. Angels and enemy priests really gave me the
worst beatings, but I managed to find a balance between finding when to
fight them (or zap them) and when to just run for it. They brutalized
my guardian Angel pretty quickly. Had totally bad instincts with
finding the altar--found Lawful first and then Neutral. I was terrified
when Death caught up with me and I couldn't get out of melee range, but
it turns out he's pretty vulnerable to Magicbane's special effects, and
I killed him pretty easily.

Magicbane's abilities also had an amusing side effect--a number of
creatures had items of create monster, but I had managed to confuse
them with Magicbane, so they summoned hordes of acid blobs. This
actually made my time in the Astral Plane slightly easier, as the blobs
blocked the path of creatures trying to chase me. Maybe I should try
this tactic more intentionally next time, summoning the blobs myself,
in difficult areas.

After getting past death and Fingering a few priests in my way, I
booked it for the Chaotic altar and took my prize.

One thing that I managed to do that I'd been bad at was inventory
management--I worked really, really hard to keep myself unburdened at
all times. Gauntlets of Power and Bag of Holding helped of course (I
originally didn't want to keep the GoP but eventually I became a strong
enough spellcaster it wasn't impinging on my ability to cast that much
and it was nice to have the extra strength). You'll see from below I
still had eight million items I really didn't need, but trust me, this
is far better than I was accomplishing before.

I've also learned that enchanting your armor is really, really, really
even more important that I thought. Not that I ever downplayed it, but
still. Finally, having Identify as a spell is an absolute godsend, and
saved me from my impatience if nothing else.

